{"title":"Course Guide","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Course Guide"},"headingText":"TRACE","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\nTRACE is the shared learning message of the course, not a topic or a software tool.\n\n> **Predict → Encounter → Probe → Explain → Decide → Verify**\n\nYou will use the same cycle on different objects: a news claim, search result, recommendation, algorithmic decision, LLM response, prompt, citation, policy, or professional case.\n\n## Weekly rhythm\n\nEvery ordinary teaching week contains four persistent components:\n\n| Component | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| **Pre-Class Quiz** | Make preparation visible and activate prior knowledge |\n| **TRACE Lab** | Experience, investigate, manipulate, explain, and verify a real case |\n| **After-Class Task** | Produce individual evidence of transfer |\n| **Next on DSA261** | Establish the shared reading/viewing culture for the next week |\n\n## Official class schedule\n\nDSA261 is scheduled on **Friday in G1-01** as three 40-minute class periods:\n\n| Time | Phase | Typical activity |\n|---|---|---|\n| **11:00–11:40** | Session 1 | cold case, prediction, encounter, focused concept, guided investigation |\n| **11:40–11:50** | Short break | — |\n| **11:50–12:30** | Session 2 | probing, information seeking, guided technical practice |\n| **12:30–13:30** | Lunch break | — |\n| **13:30–14:10** | Session 3 | pair challenge, decision, verification, evidence capture, next-week briefing |\n\nAlthough the course is formally listed as theoretical, teaching takes place in the computer laboratory. The design therefore treats each class period as an active TRACE session rather than as a continuous lecture.\n\nStudents should normally perform an observable action at least every 10–15 minutes.\n\n## Weekly Tasks\n\nWeekly Tasks are not essays. They are evidence records showing how you searched, prompted, probed, verified, and decided.\n\nAI use is permitted unless a specific task says otherwise. However:\n\n> **AI output is not verification evidence.**\n\n## Assessment direction\n\n- **Week 7:** TRACE Midterm Challenge synthesising W1–W6 evidence and skills.\n- **Weeks 12–13:** Final Project Gate 1 and Gate 2; the project scope and evidence protocol are progressively fixed.\n- **Week 14:** course review, transfer challenge, and final readiness audit.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## TRACE\n\nTRACE is the shared learning message of the course, not a topic or a software tool.\n\n> **Predict → Encounter → Probe → Explain → Decide → Verify**\n\nYou will use the same cycle on different objects: a news claim, search result, recommendation, algorithmic decision, LLM response, prompt, citation, policy, or professional case.\n\n## Weekly rhythm\n\nEvery ordinary teaching week contains four persistent components:\n\n| Component | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| **Pre-Class Quiz** | Make preparation visible and activate prior knowledge |\n| **TRACE Lab** | Experience, investigate, manipulate, explain, and verify a real case |\n| **After-Class Task** | Produce individual evidence of transfer |\n| **Next on DSA261** | Establish the shared reading/viewing culture for the next week |\n\n## Official class schedule\n\nDSA261 is scheduled on **Friday in G1-01** as three 40-minute class periods:\n\n| Time | Phase | Typical activity |\n|---|---|---|\n| **11:00–11:40** | Session 1 | cold case, prediction, encounter, focused concept, guided investigation |\n| **11:40–11:50** | Short break | — |\n| **11:50–12:30** | Session 2 | probing, information seeking, guided technical practice |\n| **12:30–13:30** | Lunch break | — |\n| **13:30–14:10** | Session 3 | pair challenge, decision, verification, evidence capture, next-week briefing |\n\nAlthough the course is formally listed as theoretical, teaching takes place in the computer laboratory. The design therefore treats each class period as an active TRACE session rather than as a continuous lecture.\n\nStudents should normally perform an observable action at least every 10–15 minutes.\n\n## Weekly Tasks\n\nWeekly Tasks are not essays. They are evidence records showing how you searched, prompted, probed, verified, and decided.\n\nAI use is permitted unless a specific task says otherwise. However:\n\n> **AI output is not verification evidence.**\n\n## Assessment direction\n\n- **Week 7:** TRACE Midterm Challenge synthesising W1–W6 evidence and skills.\n- **Weeks 12–13:** Final Project Gate 1 and Gate 2; the project scope and evidence protocol are progressively fixed.\n- **Week 14:** course review, transfer challenge, and final readiness audit.\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":"auto","echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":true,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","css":["assets/styles.css"],"toc":true,"toc-depth":